From d6bd013ba7c7c7fe5a08e59cf0dfdf21919df060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] 3D: subtitles and the interface in front
 of what the picture shows, where the video gives no depth

With the measure and the planner of the commits before, a 3D video that
carries no depth for its subtitles (MV-HEVC, side by side, top and
bottom, an MVC stream without plane offsets) has its subtitles, and the
interface drawn over it, placed in front of the nearest thing of the
picture.

- CRenderManager owns a CStereoDepthMeter: each eye's video is copied
  right after it is drawn (Render(), after ServiceVideoCaptures()), and
  once a frame (FrameMove(), after PrepareOverlays()) the depths of the
  frame are given to the overlay renderer and the graphic context.
- OVERLAY::CRenderer: SetMeasuredSubtitleDepth(); SubtitleDepth() takes
  it where the disc gives the subtitles no offset, half of it to each
  eye, as a share of the picture as drawn. The disc's offsets come
  first, its menus keep the setting, and nothing moves in 2D or in the
  mono view. GetSubtitleEvent(): a subtitle is another one where the set
  of bitmaps on screen changes or libass draws another text (its change
  2), and the place of the last ones drawn, around which the depth is
  measured.
- CGraphicContext::SetGuiDepthOverVideo() and ApplyGuiDepthOverVideo():
  a shift of each eye's interface, added to the skin's depth of each
  control, from the controls of the full-screen video window on (after
  the video and its subtitles) and for the dialogs over it, in both
  passes of the front-to-back rendering; NoteGuiOverVideo(): whether
  anything is drawn over the video, so that its depth is chosen as it
  opens and kept while it is open.
- The setting "Depth of subtitles and menus over 3D video"
  (subtitles.hadesstereodepth, Player > Subtitles, Expert): Automatic
  (the default) measures, and the depth of "Stereoscopic 3D depth of
  subtitles" is added in front of the measured one; Fixed is Kodi's
  way, that setting alone. New strings #62390 to #62392, translated in
  Estuary (#54390 to #54392: es_es, es_ar, es_mx).

Where it is not measured (an anaglyph output, an HDR video, a setting
of Fixed), everything is as before.
