diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 2c5ce4e..ad6bb76 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -28182,3 +28182,21 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#62451"
 msgid "For films wider than the screen, such as 2.39:1 on a 16:9 TV: subtitles go into the black bar under the picture, so that they never cover it. Hades finds the bar itself: from the Dolby Vision data of a video that has it, otherwise by measuring the picture (in a bright scene, a few seconds after the film starts; dark scenes and fades never move the subtitles, and when an IMAX scene fills more of the screen they move back up at once). Two lines must fit in the bar at your subtitle size: at a size of 38 or less they fit the bar of a 2.39:1 film on a 16:9 screen, at 34 or less that of a 2.35:1 one; otherwise subtitles stay where they are. Text subtitles and picture subtitles (Blu-ray PGS) both go there; subtitles that you place yourself (Position on screen: Manual) or at the top, styled ASS subtitles and 3D videos are left as they are. Off by default."
 msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: label of setting "subtitles.hadesstereodepth"; translated in Estuary (#54390)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#62390"
+msgid "Depth of subtitles and menus over 3D video"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "subtitles.hadesstereodepth"; translated in Estuary (#54391)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#62391"
+msgid "For a 3D video that carries no depth for its subtitles: MV-HEVC (spatial video, 3D films for the Vision Pro), side by side, top and bottom, and 3D Blu-ray video without plane offsets. Automatic (the default): Hades measures how near the nearest thing in the picture is where the subtitles are shown, and puts each subtitle just in front of it, so that nothing in the picture stands out in front of the text. A subtitle never jumps while it is shown, only comes forward smoothly where something comes nearer, and never comes nearer than a comfortable limit. The menus and the player information drawn over the video are placed the same way as they open, and stay where they are while open. The depth set below (Stereoscopic 3D depth of subtitles) is added in front of the measured one. Fixed: subtitles at the depth set below alone, and the menus at the skin's depth, as in Kodi. The plane offsets of a 3D Blu-ray always come first. Measured only with a 3D output that draws each eye as a picture of its own (side by side, top and bottom, frame packing), not with anaglyph, nor with HDR video. Applies at once."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of setting "subtitles.hadesstereodepth": the depth of the setting "subtitles.stereoscopicdepth" alone, as in Kodi; translated in Estuary (#54392)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#62392"
+msgid "Fixed"
+msgstr ""
